2026-11-04T02:35:51.4980783Z 
2026-11-04T02:35:51.4982761Z **One finding worth flagging to you.** `check.sh --part 2/4` is red on this runner on a step belonging to dev's T-3088 transport code, not to T-2388: `socket_controls.py`'s `orient()` uses `np.cross` on 2-vectors, which NumPy has removed. Measured both ways — numpy 2.3.5 returns `1.0` with a DeprecationWarning, numpy 2.5.4 raises. CI pins Python 3.11 (numpy 2.3.x) and is green; the steward runner has Python 3.14 (numpy 2.5.4) and is red. Part 2/4 passes here too under `numpy<2.4`. I deliberately did not fix it — `socket_controls.py` is T-3088's source and T-3088 is live, so fixing it inside a T-2388 PR would bundle unrelated work. Filed as **T-3368** (`--by loop`, effort S) with the measurement and acceptance written in. Any run gating locally on this image will hit it and shouldn't read it as its own.
